# Summary: Pi artifact commands

`dev artifacts` owns the durable artifact model. Pi only transports tool calls
and formats records for the agent; the shell picker consumes the same records.

## Storage

Artifacts for a project live at:

    $XDG_STATE_HOME/pi-artifacts/<hash>/     default ~/.local/state
      <slug>.<ext>     artifact files
      .index.json      optional title/type metadata

`<hash>` is the first 16 hex characters of the sha256 of the git top-level, or
of the physical supplied path outside a repository. The filesystem is the
source of truth: non-dotfiles that are regular files are artifacts. The sidecar
only enriches a listing. New directories are mode `0700`.

## Commands

- `dir [path]`: print the absolute artifact directory without creating it.
- `path <name> [path]`: print the absolute destination for a name without
  creating it.
- `save [--content-file=FILE] [--title=TITLE] [--type=TYPE] <name> [path]`:
  write content and optionally update passed metadata fields. Without
  `--content-file`, reads non-empty stdin.
- `delete <name> [path]`: remove an existing artifact and its sidecar entry.
- `list [--format=tsv|json] [path]`: list artifacts newest first. TSV is for
  the picker; JSON preserves metadata exactly for pi.
- `browse [path]`: choose a listed artifact in fzf. Enter opens it, `ctrl-d`
  confirms deletion, `ctrl-r` refreshes the list, and Esc exits.

`path`, `save`, and `delete` print exactly one absolute path on success. `list`
prints records or `[]` in JSON mode. Diagnostics go to stderr.

## Completions

`delete`, `path` and `save` complete `<name>` with the artifacts of the
directory being completed, taken from the first column of `list`. The optional
`[path]` argument is never completed, because `sub` only completes required
positionals. `sub` only reads an `Options:` comment block that comes before any
extended documentation, so these commands document their arguments there
instead of in an `Arguments:` block.

## Naming and metadata

Names are trimmed, reduced to their final `/` or `\` path component, stripped
of leading dots, then slugged. The stem lowercases ASCII, turns runs outside
`[a-z0-9._-]` into `-`, collapses hyphens, and trims edge dots and hyphens. The
extension is the final dot suffix, lowercased to `[a-z0-9]`, defaulting to `md`.
Invalid or escaping names fail. The CLI also checks the resulting path remains
inside the project directory.

The sidecar is a two-space-indented JSON object keyed by filename. `save` and
`delete` lock `.index.lock` while changing it, so concurrent saves preserve both
entries. Updates use a same-directory temp file and rename. A missing sidecar
is normal. A corrupt or non-object sidecar is moved to
`.index.json.corrupt.<epoch>`, warned about, and replaced rather than silently
erasing metadata. `list` fails loudly when its sidecar cannot be read.
